227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428088 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1031 "Expressing Rational Functions with Repeated Factors as Sums of Partial Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1033 1062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1034 1.0467087634404137 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050964 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "75ee3078-0f47-5483-b8f1-4f83224062ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050974 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050974 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050974 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186203971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050974 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186203972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050974 #edb/ref 1031 "Proving Consecutive Angle Theorems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050974 #edb/ref 1033 5137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050974 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "768e71db-20fc-5eea-91f6-8fb5dba99116" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050984 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050984 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050984 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050984 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050984 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Systems of Nonlinear Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050984 #edb/ref 1033 410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050984 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "76fdc42b-abcd-5aad-8530-c965d0b74cc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1031 "Linear Combinations of Vectors and Their Properties" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1033 1105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "79fb6a4f-4564-5155-81f6-db81bd65e488" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073445 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073445 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y=4 \\\\ x+2y=16\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073445 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9aae52c-65f3-5dff-bc6b-a530f8c7acc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073445 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $x$ by adding $y$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y & =4 \\\\ x & =4+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we replace $x$ with $4+y$ in the second equation and solve for $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\tx+2y &=16 \\\n\t(4+y) + 2y &=16\\\n\t4+3y &=16\\\n\t3y &=12\\\n\ty &=4\n}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=4$ into $x=4+y$, then we can find the value of $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\tx &= 4 + y \\\n\t   &= 4 + (4) \\\n\t   &=8\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x = 8$ and $y = 4$, which can be written as $(8, 4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073446 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073446 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2u+9v-6=0 \\\\ 2u+6v-8=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073446 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "707504e8-a367-5dc2-a663-371a9dcf7224" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073446 #edb/ref 1074 "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n![](images/77/77459b19bb1fd1f28e05e6f613e4e49af34595eae33eeeca584d65a289f7ea2c.svg)\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $u$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2u+6v-8 &= 0 \\\n2u+6v &= 8 \\\n2u &= 8 - 6v \\\nu &= \\dfrac{8-6v}{2} \\\nu &= 4 - 3v\n}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $u=4-3v$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $v\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2u+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n\t2(4-3v)+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n\t8-6v+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n2+3v &= 0 \\\n3v &= -2 \\\nv &= -\\dfrac{2}{3}\n}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $v=-\\dfrac{2}{3}$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $u\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t2u+9v-6 &= 0 \\\n\t2u+9\\left(-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right) -6 &= 0 \\\n\t2u-6-6 &= 0 \\\n\t2u-12 &= 0 \\\n\t2u &= 12 \\\n\tu &= 6\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=6$ and $v=-\\dfrac{2}{3}$, which can be written as $\\left(6,-\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073752 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186073997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186073998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073753 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186074657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1050 660.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073923 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "7809af08-83ac-5450-986d-2614a3fd22d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074657 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074657 #edb/ref 1061 197419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074657 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "413b9b90-7693-5568-a868-970271a5a258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074657 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186075033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074658 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074658 #edb/ref 1061 197420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074658 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "99e9f36f-648c-5025-bfca-c63f6f77d9b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074658 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074659 #edb/ref 1061 197424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074659 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30b3f613-45c5-50c5-bd79-5c12149aea27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074659 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075033 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to solve, *without* using graphs, the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y=4 \\\\ x-2=y\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to solve the system without a graph, we will need to combine the equations into a single equation that can be solved using algebraic manipulation.\n\nOne way to combine the equations is called the **substitution method.** To use the substitution method, we substitute for one variable in terms of the other.\n\nFor instance, notice that we can make $y$ the subject of the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\color{red}y=x - 2\n$$\n\nSubstituting this expression for $y$ into the first equation, we get an equation that we can solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =4 \\\\ x+(x-2) & =4 \\\\ 2x-2 & =4 \\\\ 2x & =6 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x=3.$ But we also need to figure out what $y$ is. We can do this by substituting $x=3$ back into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x-2 \\\\ y & =3-2 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x = 3$ and $y = 1$, which can be written as $\\left(3, 1\\right).$\n\n**Note:** Whenever we isolate the variable in one equation, we have to substitute it into the *other* equation. We cannot substitute a variable into the same equation it came from, because this will not give us any more information about the variable." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075033 #edb/ref 1065 8131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075033 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e1e8cb2d-3d4e-5cb9-8947-2bd9deb11b89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075033 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495509 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495509 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495509 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "001fa025-6178-5ba4-b287-f99d23255489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495542 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495542 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495542 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0db68d80-560b-5294-a3e9-812966c11801" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495696 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495696 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495696 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "51c5dada-d996-51cf-94d1-ca897ceda4c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495753 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495753 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495753 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6ed3f880-96ed-5fd6-824f-be81fbff3e25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495833 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495833 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495833 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "92cf3e39-98db-564f-a3c5-ad104dff9377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495899 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495899 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495899 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "adefce60-eb41-5a32-906f-e3cd671a3daa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495919 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495919 