186496180 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496180 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496180 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ca46e4e1-5150-5d40-98c3-33efe3175aed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186496070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496187 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496187 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496187 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186496070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496187 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d502feb6-12a4-5b5d-a239-789af82850e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496191 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186496013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496191 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496191 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496191 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186496013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496191 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d81fe473-caed-55d0-ae06-56890f9a6929" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496194 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496194 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496194 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496194 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496194 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "da300820-d65a-54b5-a122-648e1be4ca42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496198 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496198 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496198 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496198 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496198 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e16e42d5-5e57-5702-bb36-98fb0bad0dd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496207 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186495929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496207 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496207 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496207 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186495929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496207 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ef8a675b-4a10-5910-adfc-f84ccbe5facf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496226 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496226 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496226 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496226 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496226 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u-6v=-3 \\\\ u=-v-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496226 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07b5302b-d797-5328-827e-aa28a460f929" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496226 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It so happens that the second equation is already solved for $u:$\n\n$$\nu=-v-2\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $u$ with $-v-2$ in the first equation and solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u-6v & =-3 \\\\ 4(-v-2)-6v & =-3 \\\\ -4v-8-6v & =-3 \\\\ -10v & =5 \\\\ v & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $v=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into $u=-v-2,$ then we can find the value of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =-v-2 \\\\ u & =-(-\\frac{1}{2})-2 \\\\ u & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=-\\frac{3}{2},\\,v=-\\frac{1}{2},$ which can be expressed as $(-\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496252 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496252 #edb/ref 1069 "q-112214" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496252 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496252 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $y-x?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y=0 \\\\ 5y-15x+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496252 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "498d2b3f-6756-59df-bd3d-256bb722b0aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496252 #edb/ref 1074 "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y=0 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5y-15x+10=0 & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can isolate $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-15x+10 & =0 \\\\ 5y & =15x-10 \\\\ y & =3x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $3x-2$  into equation $(1)$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21x-9y & =0 \\\\ 21x-9(3x-2) & =0 \\\\ 21x-27x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6x+18 & =0 \\\\ 18 & =6x \\\\ 3 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=3$ into $y=3x-2,$ then we can find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-2 \\\\ y & =3(3)-2 \\\\ y & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3,\\,y=7.$ So,\n\n$$\ny-x=7-3=4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496255 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496255 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496255 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181175" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496255 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496255 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=-4 \\\\ x-3y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496255 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c3907fe-c83e-5bd5-ac54-297aa503451b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496255 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the second equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $x$ by adding $3y$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\nx=3y-8\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $x$ with $3y-8$ in the first equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =-4 \\\\ -2(3y-8)+y & =-4 \\\\ -6y+16+y & =-4 \\\\ -5y & =-20 \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=4$ into $x=3y-8,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3y-8 \\\\ x & =3(4)-8 \\\\ x & =12-8 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=4,\\,y=4,$ which can be expressed as $(4,4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496314 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496314 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496314 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181207" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496314 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496314 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q=-18 \\\\ 4p+3q+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(p,q)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(p,q)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496314 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d389f84f-6df2-5d57-9702-acb625d9c80f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496314 #edb/ref 1074 "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q=-18 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 4p+3q+2=0 & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(1),$ we can solve for $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6q & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =6q-18 \\\\ p & =2q-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=2q-6$ into equation $(2)$ and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2q-6)+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 8q-24+3q+2 & =0 \\\\ 11q & =22 \\\\ q & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $q=2$ into equation $(1),$ then we can find the value of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-6(2) & =-18 \\\\ 3p-12 & =-18 \\\\ 3p & =-6 \\\\ p & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-2,\\,q=2,$ which can be expressed as $(-2,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
